 "discussion": "SYNOPSIS\n\nThe southwesterly flow between a trough of low pressure on the coast and a ridge over Alberta is poised to carry a number of disturbances over the resort through most of the week ahead. Mainly cloudy conditions with intervals of snow will be punctuated by brief breaks of sunshine between systems.\n\nEXTENDED OUTLOOK\n\nTuesday to Thursday: Mainly cloudy conditions continue through Thursday as a series of disturbances are ejected into the interior from a succession of coastal storms. Periods of light snow with minor accumulations are possible each day. Maximum temperatures in the Alpine will be near minus 5°C on Tuesday, minus 4°C on Wednesday and minus 3C on Thursday as the flow gradually warms. Village highs will be near minus 1°C on Tuesday and Wednesday before rising to near zero on Thursday. Winds will increase on Tuesday to southeasterly 20-25 km/h and maintain southeast 20-25 km/h on Wednesday and Thursday.",
